      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that is generally what PDFium wants to do. However, from experience, the Chromium Clang rolls oftentimes involve more than just purely updating //tools/clang and the GCS DEPS entries. Which is why I\u0027m saying the auto-roller won\u0027t actually succeed. What can happen is a PDFium developer can clone the auto-roller\u0027s failed CL to get a head start, and then patch that up with all the other bits, .e.g third_party/abseil, to make a CL that will pass try bots.",
      "parentUuid": "a1c1a989_c23e3d1a",
